+/// What a near miss of a word in a hit's own name adds to its rank
+/// ([`near_miss_bonus`]): less than a word adds that is in the name as
+/// typed, and enough to list the name that was meant ahead of the paths that
+/// have the word's letters in order by accident.
+const NEAR_NAME: i32 = 30;
+
+/// The fewest letters of a word whose near miss in a name is ranked up. One
+/// typo in four or five letters leaves three or four of them to go by, and
+/// many names have those side by side by chance: `lens.svg` and `icon.icns`
+/// are that close to `lcns`. Ranked up, they would bury what the letters
+/// find in order, which for `lcns` is `LICENSE`.
+const NEAR_NAME_LETTERS: usize = 6;
+
+/// What a near miss that is only in a folder's name takes off a hit's rank
+/// ([`near_miss_bonus`]). One near miss scores much like another, and
+/// without this `mian` lists everything in a folder named `Many` ahead of
+/// `main.rs`.
+const NEAR_FOLDER: i32 = 30;
+
+/// What [`rerank`] adds for a word that may be misspelled
+/// ([`may_be_misspelled`]) and that a hit's name doesn't have as typed. A
+/// near miss of it in the name counts for the hit, when the word is long
+/// enough to tell by, and one that is only in a folder's name counts
+/// against it. Any other hit has the word's letters in order along its
+/// path, or may spell a letter of it apart, and is left where fff-search
+/// ranks it, as every hit is when no word may be misspelled.
+///
+/// # Arguments
+///
+/// * `hit` - A hit that the search lists
+/// * `name` - Its name, in lowercase
+/// * `word` - The word, in lowercase
+fn near_miss_bonus(hit: &RawHit, name: &str, word: &str) -> i32 {
+    let typos = typo_budget(word);
+    if near_miss(word, name, typos) {
+        if word.chars().count() >= NEAR_NAME_LETTERS {
+            NEAR_NAME
+        } else {
+            0
+        }
+    } else if is_subsequence(word, &hit.rel) {
+        0
+    } else if word.is_ascii() || near_miss(word, &hit.rel, typos) {
+        // The hit is listed for a near miss, which the name doesn't have.
+        -NEAR_FOLDER
+    } else {
+        // Listed for a letter that may be spelled apart.
+        0
+    }
+}
